<title>POLAND: POLAND OFFERS PLN 800 MLN FIXED BONDS ON APRIL 2.</title>
<headline>POLAND OFFERS PLN 800 MLN FIXED BONDS ON APRIL 2.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland offered to sell 800 million zlotys of 15-percent two-year bonds and 12-percent five-year bonds at a primary tender on April 2, the central bank said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The settlement date for the auction is April 12, 1997.</p>
<p>The shorter bonds mature on June 12, 1999 and the longer ones on June 12, 2002.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
